    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) serving as our undisputed anchor. Facing a favorable matchup against Triston Rogers (4.01 xERA), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a massive park factor boost and a prime #3 lineup spot, making him our highest-ceiling asset for Roto production. Close behind is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), whose efficiency is surging due to a soft matchup against Giolito (5.37 xERA). While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** typically relies on his elite bat-to-ball skills, the high-run environment projected for this matchup against an exploitable arm positions him as a high-floor play. We are also monitoring **Sam Antonacci** (67.67), who leverages a favorable #1 batting position and a +19% SP skill advantage to remain a mandatory start for stolen base stability.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved our MI/Utility slots, specifically the benching of **Coby Mayo** (46.33). While **Coby Mayo** benefits from a strong park factor against Macko, his efficiency is cannibalized by the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill and an unfavorable #8 spot in the order. He fell just short of **Miguel Vargas** (59.40), who manages to hold value despite a slight park penalty, thanks to a higher-leverage lineup spot and better platoon alignment. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Andy Pages** (46.24) and **Kyle Tucker** (52.60); both draw the short straw against Wheeler (2.86 xERA). While **Kyle Tucker** remains locked in for his elite tools, we are heavily discounting their raw output expectations given the suppression from one of the league's most difficult arms. Keep an eye on **Liam Hicks** (46.76) and **Gunnar Henderson** (52.11), both of whom are facing SPs with xERAs under 4.00, introducing significant volatility to our early-game offensive output.",
